<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1099" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad-vīvo</span></b> , ĕre,
			v. n.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To live with one;</i> joined with cum by pleonasm: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">CONIVGI DVLCISSIMO CVM QVO ADVIXIT SINE QVERELA
					PER ANNOS XX.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 1145, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">1115, 8</span></i> (Orell. 3094).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To live</i>, with the access. idea of continuance,
				<i>to live on</i>, <i>to continue
				living</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dum adviveret,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Josh. 4, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">donec advivet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					34, 3, 28</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quamdiu advixerit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 3,
					4, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">30</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
